The key complication is that rows and sessions do not map one-to-one. `gdrom_default_probe.py` has a row that combines eight separate runs, while other sessions feed several rows. A shortcut that skips sessions and returns dummy data can therefore certify an aggregate after running only part of it.

The gate also ignores the probe’s exit status with `|| true`. A filtered run needs a distinct output protocol; a nonzero exit alone cannot keep it from being accepted.
